{
  "computation": "qbeta-discriminant-curve-in-q",
  "engine": "sympy+mpmath",
  "description": "qou-cds1 Step 26. CORRECTS a method error running through Steps 21-25: all of them evaluated spectra at the single point q = q_0, which cannot distinguish a perfect-square discriminant from an irreducible degree-18 one. Carrying q symbolically (`hm_sym`, mirroring `build_nucleon_nf`'s 11-crossing braid-order word, validated to 1e-16) gives the exact spectral curves. ALSO CORRECTS Step 25's claim that Delta_L could not be asked this question: there was no gap, only a function not looked for. Results: tr is bar-odd, det and disc bar-even as exact identities, so there is NO q^-n twist and disc is a polynomial in x = q + 1/q. disc_S(x) = x^2 - 4 = h^2 is a perfect square (genus 0) and is >= 0 for every real q, so the short model is hyperbolic everywhere, not just at q_0. disc_L(x) has degree 18, is squarefree with four irreducible factors, and y^2 = disc_L is hyperelliptic of GENUS 8 (genus 4 on the x^2 quotient) — not genus 1, so there is no elliptic curve and no tower of them. The Hecke tower adds no eigenvalue by branching, verified on all five H_4 shapes. The classical limit is EXACTLY 2 pi / 3, because the leading direction of Delta_L at q = 1 is -(1 + T_1 T_0) and T_1 T_0 is the S_3 3-cycle; the trefoil word e^- enters only at second order. Delta_L is elliptic exactly for q in (1, 1.3797326616) with q_0 29 % of the way up, and theta sweeps to 0 at the wall, so the required ladder phase IS attained — at q* = 1.3781 (z_C) / 1.3796 (z_D), both ~3e11 sigma_q0 from the calibrated q_0. The avenue is closed by the CODATA proton pin. The cyclotomic tower q = zeta_N is a genuine tower with phi_3 = phi_6 = 2 pi / 3 exactly, but its minimum over N <= 120 still exceeds the required phase by 24x.",
  "contentBlock": "def:three-calibration-discipline",
  "assertions": [
    {
      "name": "symbolic_nucleon_nf_mirrors_the_canonical_builder",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "the symbolic (2,1) irrep satisfies the Hecke and braid relations identically in q and matches the corpus Hoefsmit output at q_0 to 2.01e-35; the symbolic nucleon NF matches `build_nucleon_nf` to 9.15e-17 in all 12 coordinates. CORRECTS Step 25's claim that Delta_L could not be asked this question — `hm_sym` is the symbolic twin of `hm` and there was no gap"
    },
    {
      "name": "disc_is_bar_even_for_both_models_no_q_twist",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "tr(1/q) = -tr(q), det(1/q) = det(q), disc(1/q) = disc(q) as exact identities in Q(q). The bar involution acts trivially on the spectral geometry, so there is no q^-n twist to be missed as one goes out the tower, and disc is forced to be a polynomial in x = q + 1/q"
    },
    {
      "name": "short_model_disc_is_h_squared_hence_hyperbolic_at_every_real_q",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "disc_S(q) = h(q)^2 is a perfect square in the q coordinate and disc_S(x) = x^2 - 4 is a degree-2 conic in x, so y^2 = disc_S has genus 0 either way; and x = q + 1/q >= 2 for every real q > 0, so disc_S >= 0 identically. The short model is hyperbolic at EVERY real q, not merely at q_0 — a statement Steps 21-25 could not have made"
    },
    {
      "name": "long_model_curve_is_genus_8_not_elliptic",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "disc_L(x) = (x-2)(x+2) G_-(x) G_+(x) / 16 with G_-+ = 2x^8 - 21x^6 + 77x^4 - 115x^2 -+ 2x + 58: degree 18, squarefree, four irreducible factors over Q. y^2 = disc_L is hyperelliptic of genus 8; being even in x it covers a genus-4 curve in w = x^2. Neither is genus 1, so there is no elliptic curve and no tower of them. Both polynomials agree with the Lean mirror `QOU.QBeta.DiscriminantCurveInQ`"
    },
    {
      "name": "hecke_tower_adds_no_eigenvalue_by_branching",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "all five H_4 spectra of Delta_L are exactly the branching unions of the three H_3 spectra: (2,2)=(2,1), (3,1)=(3)+(2,1), (2,1,1)=(1^3)+(2,1), (4)=(3), (1^4)=(1^3). Every corpus object is H_3-valued, so no new discriminant appears at any level n"
    },
    {
      "name": "classical_limit_eigenphase_is_exactly_two_pi_over_three",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "every NF coordinate of Delta_L carries (q-1)(q+1), so Delta_L -> 0 at q = 1; the leading direction is -(gamma + L_-) = -(1 + T_1 T_0), and T_1 T_0 is the S_3 3-cycle whose standard-rep eigenvalues are the primitive cube roots of unity, giving modulus 1 and eigenphase exactly 2 pi / 3. The trefoil / electron word e^- enters only at order 2"
    },
    {
      "name": "ladder_phase_crossing_is_excluded_by_the_substrate_pin",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "Delta_L is elliptic exactly for q in (1, 1.3797326616) and its eigenphase sweeps from 2 pi / 3 to 0, so the required phase IS attained — at q* = 1.37812464914 (z_C) and 1.37956231361 (z_D), both within 0.2 % of the degeneracy wall and ~3e11 sigma_q0 from the calibrated q_0. Closed by the CODATA proton pin, not by inspection"
    },
    {
      "name": "cyclotomic_tower_phases_all_exceed_the_required_phase",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "on |q| = 1 the trace is purely imaginary and the determinant real (|Re tr| < 1.51e-40, |Im det| < 4.01e-42), so every root of unity carries a real discriminant and a well-defined eigenphase. This IS a genuine tower indexed by the degree N, with phi_3 = phi_6 = 2 pi / 3 exactly and phi_N -> 2 pi / 3 as N -> infinity; its minimum over N <= 120 is phi_7 = 1.4042283, still 24.812x the required phase"
    }
  ],
